       restores 0x02 -- the release lives only in the SMU
       session (re-run --manual-powerup after any cold cycle).
    -> rail = 0: IDLE -- the rail-up bit self-clears when the
       sequencer takes it, so 0 carries no state by itself
       (powered dom0-3 also read 0). MEASURED 2026-08-25: the
       rail-up store landed (the ctrl store in the same run
       did) yet moved nothing -- favored reading: an already-
       up rail consumed the one-shot instantly. The SMU-side
       power question is as settled as this oracle can make
